  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Differentiation [S+N]\n\nThe **derivative** is the limit of secant slopes:\n\n$$f'(x_0) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(x_0 + h) - f(x_0)}{h}.$$\n\nWhen the limit exists, $f$ is differentiable at $x_0$. Two consequences land immediately:\n\n- Differentiable ⇒ continuous (the converse fails — see Weierstrass).\n- The tangent line at $(x_0, f(x_0))$ has slope $f'(x_0)$.\n\nThis notebook does the concrete: visualise the limit-of-secants, illustrate the **mean value theorem** (the workhorse of real analysis), and study **Taylor's theorem** with explicit Lagrange remainder.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 64,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Secant slopes converging to the tangent slope\n\nTake $f(x) = \\sin(x)$ at $x_0 = 1$. Compute secant slopes for shrinking $h$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f(x) := sin(x)$\nx0 : 1.0$\nh_vals : [1.0, 0.5, 0.1, 0.01, 0.001, 0.0001]$\nsecants : map(lambda([h], float((f(x0 + h) - f(x0)) / h)), h_vals)$\n\nprint(\"h values:        \", h_vals)$\nprint(\"secant slopes:   \", secants)$\nprint(\"true derivative: cos(1) =\", float(cos(x0)))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 65,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "h values:         [1.0,0.5,0.1,0.01,0.001,1.0e-4]\nsecant slopes:\n                 [0.0678264420177852,0.3120480035923159,0.4973637525353891,\n                  0.536085981011869,0.5398814803603269,0.5402602314186211]\ntrue derivative: cos(1) = 0.5403023058681398"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The tangent line as the limit of secants\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "x_grid : np_to_list(np_linspace(-0.5, 2.5, 200))$\ny_grid : map(lambda([x], float(f(x))), x_grid)$\nderiv_x0 : float(cos(x0))$\ny0 : float(f(x0))$\n\n/* tangent: y = y0 + deriv*(x - x0) */\ny_tangent : map(lambda([x], y0 + deriv_x0 * (x - x0)), x_grid)$\n/* one secant for h=0.5 */\nh_show : 0.5$\nslope_sec : float((f(x0 + h_show) - y0) / h_show)$\ny_secant : map(lambda([x], y0 + slope_sec * (x - x0)), x_grid)$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=2, name=\"f(x) = sin(x)\",\n  lines(x_grid, y_grid),\n  color=\"green\", line_width=1, name=\"secant (h = 0.5)\",\n  lines(x_grid, y_secant),\n  color=\"red\", line_width=2, name=\"tangent (h → 0)\",\n  lines(x_grid, y_tangent),\n  marker_size=6, color=\"black\",\n  points([x0, x0 + h_show], [y0, float(f(x0 + h_show))]),\n  title=\"As h → 0 the secant rotates into the tangent\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"y\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 66,
      "outputs": [
        {
