    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Mean Value Theorem [S+N]\n\nIf $f$ is continuous on $[a, b]$ and differentiable on $(a, b)$, there exists $c \\in (a, b)$ such that\n\n$$f'(c) = \\frac{f(b) - f(a)}{b - a}.$$\n\nGeometrically: somewhere on the curve, the **tangent is parallel to the chord** through the endpoints. We can find $c$ symbolically with Maxima.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "g_sym : x^3 - 2*x$\na_pt : 0$ b_pt : 2$\ng_a : subst(x = a_pt, g_sym)$\ng_b : subst(x = b_pt, g_sym)$\nchord_slope : (g_b - g_a) / (b_pt - a_pt)$\nprint(\"chord slope =\", chord_slope)$\n\ng_prime : diff(g_sym, x)$\nprint(\"g'(x) =\", g_prime)$\nc_solns : solve(g_prime = chord_slope, x)$\nprint(\"c such that g'(c) = chord slope:\", c_solns)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 67,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "chord slope = 2\ng'(x) = 3*x^2-2\nc such that g'(c) = chord slope: [x = -(2/sqrt(3)),x = 2/sqrt(3)]"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Plot the curve, the chord, and the parallel tangent.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "g_func(x) := x^3 - 2*x$\nx_g : np_to_list(np_linspace(-0.2, 2.2, 200))$\ny_g : map(lambda([x], float(g_func(x))), x_g)$\n\nc_val : float(rhs(c_solns[2]))$  /* the positive root in (0, 2) */\nslope_val : float(chord_slope)$\ng_c : float(g_func(c_val))$\n\ny_chord   : map(lambda([x], float(g_a) + slope_val * (x - a_pt)), x_g)$\ny_tan_par : map(lambda([x], g_c     + slope_val * (x - c_val)), x_g)$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=2, name=\"g(x) = x³ - 2x\",\n  lines(x_g, y_g),\n  color=\"green\", line_width=1, name=\"chord\",\n  lines(x_g, y_chord),\n  color=\"red\", line_width=2, name=\"tangent at c (parallel to chord)\",\n  lines(x_g, y_tan_par),\n  marker_size=8, color=\"black\", name=\"(a, g(a)), (b, g(b))\",\n  points([float(a_pt), float(b_pt)], [float(g_a), float(g_b)]),\n  marker_size=8, color=\"orange\", name=\"(c, g(c))\",\n  points([c_val], [g_c]),\n  title=\"Mean Value Theorem — c exists where tangent ∥ chord\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"g(x)\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 68,
      "outputs": [
        {
