    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Taylor's theorem with Lagrange remainder [S+N]\n\nIf $f$ is $(n+1)$-times continuously differentiable on an interval containing $a$ and $x$, then\n\n$$f(x) = \\underbrace{\\sum_{k=0}^{n} \\frac{f^{(k)}(a)}{k!}\\,(x-a)^k}_{P_n(x)} + \\underbrace{\\frac{f^{(n+1)}(\\xi)}{(n+1)!}\\,(x-a)^{n+1}}_{R_n(x)}$$\n\nfor some $\\xi$ between $a$ and $x$. The polynomial part $P_n$ is the **Taylor approximation**; the remainder $R_n$ is its error. Maxima computes $P_n$ symbolically.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f_taylor : exp(x)$\nn_terms : [1, 2, 4, 6]$\nexpansions : map(lambda([N], taylor(f_taylor, x, 0, N)), n_terms)$\nfor i : 1 thru length(n_terms) do\n  print(\"P_\", n_terms[i], \"(x) =\", expansions[i])$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 69,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "P_ 1 (x) = 1+x\nP_ 2 (x) = 1+x+x^2/2\nP_ 4 (x) = 1+x+x^2/2+x^3/6+x^4/24\nP_ 6 (x) = 1+x+x^2/2+x^3/6+x^4/24+x^5/120+x^6/720"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Plot the partial Taylor approximations of $e^x$ around 0 against the truth on $[-2, 2]$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "x_t : np_to_list(np_linspace(-2, 2, 200))$\ny_truth : map(lambda([x], float(exp(x))), x_t)$\ny_p1 : map(lambda([xx], float(subst(x = xx, expand(expansions[1])))), x_t)$\ny_p2 : map(lambda([xx], float(subst(x = xx, expand(expansions[2])))), x_t)$\ny_p4 : map(lambda([xx], float(subst(x = xx, expand(expansions[3])))), x_t)$\ny_p6 : map(lambda([xx], float(subst(x = xx, expand(expansions[4])))), x_t)$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"black\", line_width=2, name=\"e^x (truth)\",\n  lines(x_t, y_truth),\n  color=\"red\", line_width=1, name=\"P₁\",\n  lines(x_t, y_p1),\n  color=\"orange\", line_width=1, name=\"P₂\",\n  lines(x_t, y_p2),\n  color=\"green\", line_width=1, name=\"P₄\",\n  lines(x_t, y_p4),\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=1, name=\"P₆\",\n  lines(x_t, y_p6),\n  title=\"Taylor approximations of e^x at 0 — error shrinks with order\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"y\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 70,
      "outputs": [
