    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Numerical convergence of the remainder\n\nLagrange's bound: $|R_n(x)| \\le \\dfrac{M_{n+1}}{(n+1)!}\\,|x-a|^{n+1}$ where $M_{n+1} = \\sup_{\\xi}|f^{(n+1)}(\\xi)|$. For $e^x$ at $a = 0$ on $[-2, 2]$, $M_{n+1} = e^2 \\approx 7.39$ and the bound shrinks **factorially** in $n$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "M : float(exp(2))$  /* sup |e^ξ| on [0, 2] */\nx_eval : 2.0$\nn_orders : [1, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10]$\nerrs_actual : []$ errs_bound : []$\nfor n in n_orders do block([Pn, val_Pn, err, bnd],\n  Pn : taylor(exp(x), x, 0, n),\n  val_Pn : float(subst(x = x_eval, expand(Pn))),\n  err : abs(float(exp(x_eval)) - val_Pn),\n  bnd : M * x_eval^(n+1) / float((n+1)!),\n  errs_actual : endcons(err, errs_actual),\n  errs_bound  : endcons(bnd, errs_bound))$\nprint(\"n:                \", n_orders)$\nprint(\"actual |R_n(2)|:  \", errs_actual)$\nprint(\"Lagrange bound:   \", errs_bound)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 71,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "n:                 [1,2,4,6,8,10]\nactual |R_n(2)|:\n                  [4.38905609893065,2.3890560989306504,0.3890560989306504,\n                   0.033500543375095226,0.0017545116290635931,\n                   6.138993594273501e-5]\nLagrange bound:\n                  [14.7781121978613,9.8520747985742,1.9704149597148402,\n                   0.18765856759188954,0.010425475977327197,\n                   3.791082173573526e-4]"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Differentiable but not C¹\n\nA subtle pathology: $f(x) = x^2 \\sin(1/x)$ for $x \\ne 0$, $f(0) = 0$. It's differentiable everywhere — but $f'$ is discontinuous at 0. Differentiability and continuity of the derivative are not the same condition.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "x_pat : np_to_list(np_linspace(-0.3, 0.3, 2000))$\ny_pat : map(lambda([x], if x = 0.0 then 0.0 else float(x*x*sin(1/x))), x_pat)$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=1, name=\"x² sin(1/x)\",\n  lines(x_pat, y_pat),\n  title=\"Differentiable everywhere, but f'(0) defined while f' itself is discontinuous\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"f(x)\",\n  grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 72,
