    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The Mean Value Theorem and Taylor's theorem are the two engines that drive most of single-variable calculus — error bounds for numerical methods, optimisation conditions, the inverse function theorem, and the asymptotic analysis of all sorts of approximations.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
